 "title": "Sheridan County Treasurer",
 "text": "Sheridan County Treasurer\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nVirtual Nebraska\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's Office\nGIS Workshop\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nProperty Valuation Protests\nSpecial Licenses\nCounty Court Office\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict Court Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's Office\nSecretary of State\nLocal Election Results\nExtension\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nProbation\nPublic Defender\nPublic Transportation\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's Office\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's Exam\nDrivers Licenses\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nGeneral Links\nOther Organizations\nTreasurer\nOffice Hours\n8:00 am - 4:15 pm\nMonday - Thursday\n8:00 am - 12:45 pm\nFriday\nExcluding Federal and State Holidays.\nPLEASE NOTE - The Treasurer does not issue titles:\nMonday - Thursday after 4:00 pm\nor Friday after 12:30 pm\nPhone\n308-327-5651\nDMV: 1-308-327-2902\nAddress\nCourthouse\nPO Box 570\n301 E 2nd Street\nRushville, NE 69360\nEmail\ntreasurer@sheridancounty.ne.gov\nTax Sale\nPublic Tax Sale Registration Form\nForm W-9\nPublic Delinquent Tax Sale List Provided by Nebraska Taxes Online\nLinks\nNebraska Taxes Online\nRenew License Plates\nwww.clickdmv.ne.gov\nDriver's Exam Schedule\nTreasurer FAQ\nDrivers Licenses\nDMV Nebraska\nApplication Forms\nUnclaimed\nProperty\nState Treasurer\nUnclaimed Property Form\nUnclaimed Property FAQ\nBoating Registrations\nProperty Tax Payment Information\nRenee E. Thies\n|\nTreasurer\n|\nThe Sheridan County Treasurer’s Office is located on the main floor of the Courthouse. It is the first office on your right when you come in the\nfront door. This is the place to go if you want to pay your taxes or register an automobile or boat.\nThe County Treasurer is elected to a four year term by the voters of Sheridan County and may run for additional terms. As an elected official the\nTreasurer answers directly to the citizens of the county.\nResponsibilities:\nCollect all revenues for the County\nBill and collect all real estate and personal taxes in the county\nDisburse collections to the proper political subdivisions\nRegister all motor vehicles with tax situs in the County\nIssue driver licenses, C.D.L.'s, learner permits, school permits, etc.\nApplicants for drivers licenses must see the examiner first\nYou may renew your expiring Nebraska license within 90 days (not three months) prior to the expiration date. If you move to a new\naddress, you should update your Nebraska license within 60 days. Examiners are at the Courthouse every Wednesday. 8:45 - 12:00. and 12:45 -\n4:00.\nTaxes for both Real Estate and Personal Property are due December 31st.\n1st half is delinquent the following May 1\n2nd half is delinquent the following September 1\n14% statutory interest rate is charged on delinquencies\nSemi-Annual Statements\nJanuary 2026 thru June 2026\nJuly 2025 thru December 2025\nJanuary 2025 thru June 2025\nJanuary 2024 thru June 2024\nJuly 2023 thru December 2023\nJanuary 2023 thru June 2023\nFund Balances\nDecember 2025\nNovember 2025\nOctober 2025\n-->\nSeptember 2025\nAugust 2026\nJuly 2026\nJune 2026\nMay 2026\nApril 2026\nMarch 2026\nFebruary 2026\nJanuary 2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\n2020\n2019\n|\nOperating Statements\nDecember 2025\nNovember 2025\nOctober 2025\n-->\nSeptember 2025\nAugust 2026\nJuly 2026\nJune 2026\nMay 2026\nApril 2026\nMarch 2026\nFebruary 2026\nJanuary 2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\n2020\n2019\n|\nCopyright © 2019 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
